        "original_id": "a3524a10-96a8-5baf-b17f-a81c4f0cb19b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Williams College, University of Southern California, Park Street Church\n- People: Ephraim Williams, Edward Dorr Griffin\n- Places: Williamstown, Massachusetts, California, Province of Massachusetts Bay\n- Roles: college president, pastor, minister, educator\n\nFacts:\n- Ephraim Williams was a colonist from the Province of Massachusetts Bay who was killed in the French and Indian War in 1755.\n- Edward Dorr Griffin was born on 6 January 1770 and later became a Christian minister and an American educator.\n- Williams College was established in 1793 with funds from the estate of Ephraim Williams.\n- University of Southern California was founded in 1880 and is the oldest private research university in California.\n- Edward Dorr Griffin served as the first pastor of Park Street Church from 1811 to 1815.\n- Edward Dorr Griffin served as President of Williams College from 1821 to 1836.\n- Edward Dorr Griffin died on 8 November 1837.\n- Williams College is a private liberal arts college in Williamstown, Massachusetts, United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
