        "text": "Page: Williams College. Sentence: Williams College is a private liberal arts college in Williamstown, Massachusetts, United States.\nPage: Williams College. Sentence: It was established in 1793 with funds from the estate of Ephraim Williams a colonist from the Province of Massachusetts Bay who was killed in the French and Indian War in 1755.\nPage: University of Southern California. Sentence: Founded in 1880, it is the oldest private research university in California.\nPage: Edward Dorr Griffin. Sentence: Edward Dorr Griffin (6 January 1770 – 8 November 1837) was a Christian minister and an American educator who served as President of Williams College from 1821 to 1836 and served as the first pastor of Park Street Church from 1811 to 1815.",
